Author: b <a@b>
Date:   Tue Oct 6 10:10:00 2026 -0700

    Extract the price, like we extracted messageFor
    
    The tests can't choose what the bank says: buyCoffee() makes its own
    BankCardReader, and the bank approves or declines at random.
    
    Part of buyCoffee() doesn't need the bank at all: working out the price.
    So this makes the same move as messageFor(). getPrice() is handed the
    modification and returns what to charge. It never touches the reader,
    so its tests pass every run.
    
    But the charge is still in buyCoffee(), and so is the bank's random
    answer. Extracting worked for messageFor() because what it needed from
    the clock was just a value. What buyCoffee() needs from the bank is a
    call: charging the card is buyCoffee()'s job. Passing in the bank's
    answer instead would hand that job to whoever calls buyCoffee().
    
    We want to control the bank's answer without taking away the charge.

